hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17913","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, he said, I heard Abu Salih, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to enter upon women whose husbands are absent."
"17914","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Musa narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal."
"17915","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, he said, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and said, Take your clothes and your weapons then come to me. So I came to him while he was performing ablution, and he looked me up and down, then said, I intend to send you at the head of an army, so Allah will keep you safe and grant you spoils, and I desire a good share of wealth for you. He said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, I did not become Muslim for wealth, but I became Muslim out of desire for Islam and to be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said, O Amr, good lawful wealth is excellent for a righteous man."
"17916","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said, Musa narrated to us, I heard my father say, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, and he mentioned it, and he said, he looked me up and down."
"17917","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from a man of the people of Egypt narrating from Amr ibn al-As, that he said, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr was captured and refused. So Amr kept questioning him, hoping he would claim protection. So Amr said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The lowest of the Muslims grants protection on their behalf."
"17918","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from a man of the people of Egypt narrating that Amr ibn al-As gave gifts to some people and favored Ammar ibn Yasir. He was questioned about it, so he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, The rebellious party will kill him."
"17919","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said, al-Hakam informed me, he said, I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih narrating from a freedman of Amr ibn al-As that Amr ibn al-As sent him to Ali to ask his permission to visit his wife Asma bint Umays. So he gave him permission, and they discussed a need. When the freedman left, he asked him about that, so Amr said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to seek permission to visit women except with the permission of their husbands."
"17920","Rawh narrated to us, he said, Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Abu Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani, that he entered with Abd Allah ibn Amr upon his father Amr ibn al-As, so he offered them food and said, Eat. He said, I am fasting. Amr said, Eat, for these are the days the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order us to break fast in and forbid fasting in. Malik said, and they are the days of Tashriq."
"17921","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Said ibn Kathir informed me that Jafar ibn al-Muttalib informed him that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As visited Amr ibn al-As, so he invited him to lunch, and he said, I am fasting. Then a second time likewise, then a third time likewise. So he said, No, unless you heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17922","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said, Abu Jafar al-Khatmi narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, he said, While we were with Amr ibn al-As on a Hajj or Umrah, he said, While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this mountain pass, he said, Look, do you see anything. So we said, We see crows, among them a crow with a white belly and a red beak and legs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, None of the women will enter Paradise except one like this crow among the crows."
"17923","Yazid narrated to us, Musa narrated to us, he said, I heard my father say, Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, narrated to me that Amr ibn al-As used to fast continuously, and rarely ate the evening meal at the start of the night; most of what he ate was at the pre-dawn time. He said, And I heard him say, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal."
"17924","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said, Musa narrated to us, he said, I heard my father say, I was with Amr ibn al-As in Alexandria, and they mentioned the livelihood they enjoyed. A man of the Companions said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his family never ate their fill of coarse bread. Musa said, meaning barley and sult mixed together."
"17925","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said, Musa narrated to us, he said, I heard my father say, I heard Amr ibn al-As addressing the people in Egypt, saying, How far is your conduct from the conduct of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for him, he was the most abstinent of people in this world, while you are the most desirous of people for it."
"17926","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, When the judge judges and strives and is correct, he has two rewards. And when he judges and strives and errs, he has one reward."
"17927","He said, So I narrated this hadith to Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm. He said, Thus Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah."
"17928","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, While I was asleep the angels came to me and carried the pillar of the Book from beneath my pillow and took it to al-Sham. Verily faith is where tribulations occur, in al-Sham."
"17929","Affan narrated to us, he said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said, Abu Hafs and Kulthum ibn Jabr informed us, from Abu Ghadiyah, he said, Ammar ibn Yasir was killed, so Amr ibn al-As was informed. He said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, His killer and his despoiler are in the Fire. So it was said to Amr, Yet here you are fighting him. He said, He only said, his killer and his despoiler."
"17930","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Rashid, freedman of Habib ibn Abi Aws al-Thaqafi, from Habib ibn Abi Aws, he said, Amr ibn al-As narrated to me from his own mouth, he said, When we left the Confederates at the Trench, I gathered men of Quraysh who respected my standing and listened to me. So I said to them, By Allah, you know I see the affair of Muhammad rising over all affairs with a great alarming rise. And I have formed an opinion, so what do you think of it. They said, What have you seen. He said, I think we should join al-Najashi and stay with him. If Muhammad prevails over our people we will be with al-Najashi, for to be under his hand is dearer to us than to be under the hands of Muhammad. And if our people prevail, we are men already known, and nothing but good will come to us from them. So they said, This is sound judgment. He said, So I said to them, Gather for him what we will gift him, and the most beloved gift to him from our land was leather. So we gathered much leather for him and set out until we came to him. By Allah, while we were with him, Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent him to him concerning Jafar and his companions. He said, So he entered upon him then left him. He said, So I said to my companions, This is Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri. If I enter upon al-Najashi and ask him for him and he gives him to me, I will strike his neck. If I do that, Quraysh will see that I have sufficed on their behalf by killing the messenger of Muhammad. He said, So I entered upon him and prostrated to him as I used to do. He said, Welcome to my friend, have you gifted me anything from your land. He said, I said, Yes, O king, I have gifted you much leather. He said, Then I presented it to him, and it pleased him and he desired it. Then I said to him, O king, I have seen a man leaving you, and he is the messenger of a man who is our enemy, so give him to me to kill him, for he has struck down our nobles and our best. He said, So he became angry, then stretched his hand and struck his nose with it so hard that I thought he had broken it, and had the earth split open I would have entered it out of fear of him. Then I said, O king, by Allah, had I thought you would dislike this I would not have asked you. So he said to him, Do you ask me to give you the messenger of a man to whom comes the Greatest Namus that used to come to Musa, to kill him. He said, I said, O king, is it so. So he said, Woe to you, O Amr, obey me and follow him, for by Allah he is upon the truth, and he will surely prevail over whoever opposes him as Musa prevailed over Pharaoh and his soldiers. He said, I said, Then pledge allegiance for him to me upon Islam. He said, Yes. So he stretched his hand and I pledged to him upon Islam. Then I went out to my companions with my opinion changed from what it had been, and I concealed my Islam from my companions. Then I left heading for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to become Muslim, and I met Khalid ibn al-Walid, shortly before the Conquest, coming from Makkah. So I said, Where to, O Abu Sulayman. He said, By Allah, the path has become clear, and the man is indeed a Prophet. By Allah, I go to become Muslim, so for how long. He said, I said, By Allah, I have come only to become Muslim. He said, So we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Khalid ibn al-Walid came forward and became Muslim and pledged. Then I drew near and said, O Messenger of Allah, I pledge to you on condition that you forgive my past sins, and I do not mention the later. He said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Amr, pledge, for Islam wipes away what was before it, and emigration wipes away what was before it. He said, So I pledged to him then left. Ibn Ishaq said, One whom I do not suspect narrated to me that Uthman ibn Talhah ibn Abi Talhah was with them and became Muslim when they did."
"17931","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, he said, When Ammar ibn Yasir was killed, Amr ibn Hazm entered upon Amr ibn al-As and said, Ammar has been killed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The rebellious party will kill him. So Amr ibn al-As stood up alarmed, repeating the return to Allah, until he entered upon Muawiyah. Muawiyah said to him, What is wrong with you. He said, Ammar has been killed. So Muawiyah said, Ammar has been killed, so what. Amr said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, The rebellious party will kill him. So Muawiyah said to him, You have slipped in your urine. Did we kill him. Rather Ali and his companions killed him; they brought him until they cast him between our spears, or he said, between our swords."
"17932","He said, Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Jafar ibn al-Muttalib, and he was a man of the kin of Amr ibn al-As, he said, He invited a Bedouin to food, the day after the sacrifice. The Bedouin said, I am fasting. So he said to him, Amr ibn al-As invited a man to food on this day, and he said, I am fasting. So Amr said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on this day."
"17933","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said, Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammasah narrated to him, he said, When death approached Amr ibn al-As he wept. His son Abd Allah said to him, Why do you weep, out of dread of death. So he said, No, by Allah, but because of what comes after. So he said to him, You were upon good, and he reminded him of the companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his conquests of al-Sham. So Amr said, You have left the best of all that: the testimony that there is no god but Allah. I was in three states, in none but I knew myself in it. At first I was a disbeliever, the fiercest of people against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had I died then, the Fire would have been due for me. When I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I was the shyest of people before him, so I never filled my eyes with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor questioned him about what I wanted, until he joined Allah Almighty, out of shyness before him. Had I died that day, people would have said, Congratulations to Amr, he became Muslim and was upon good, then died, and Paradise was hoped for him. Then after that I became entangled with authority and things, and I do not know whether for me or against me. When I die, do not weep over me, do not follow me with one who praises nor with fire, tighten my waist-wrapper around me, for I am a disputant, pour dust over me a pouring, for my right side is no more entitled to dust than my left side, do not put wood or stone in my grave, and when you bury me sit beside me for the time of slaughtering a camel and cutting it up, that I may find comfort with you."
"17934","Affan narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said, Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab narrated to us, he said, Amr ibn al-As showed great distress at death. When his son Abd Allah ibn Amr saw that, he said, O Abu Abd Allah, what is this distress, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bring you close and employ you. He said, O my son, that was so, and I will tell you about it. By Allah, I do not know whether that was out of love or conciliating me. But I testify concerning two men that he left this world loving them: Ibn Sumayyah and Ibn Umm Abd. When he told him, he put his hand where the collar is on his chin and said, O Allah, You commanded us and we neglected, and You forbade us and we committed, and nothing suffices us but Your forgiveness. And that was his refrain until he died."
